  "name": "rete",
  "description": "rete is a cloud-native, range-queryable RDF graph file format and engine. A `.rete` file is a single immutable artifact that answers SPARQL by HTTP range reads, so a multi-gigabyte graph is queryable from static hosting — in the browser, from the CLI, or from Python, JavaScript, R, Java and Blender — with no server and no database. An embedded Dataset Card makes each file self-describing in two small range requests at any size.",
